<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32321" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Oenōnē</span></b> ,
		ēs, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὀινώνη</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A Phrygian nymph</i>, <i>the daughter
				of Cebren</i>, <i>beloved by Paris</i>, <i>but afterwards deserted by him</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. H. 5</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Dict. Cret. 3, 21</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Suet.
				Dom. 10</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Another name for the island of Ægina</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				4, 12, 19, § 57</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
